{
  "kind": "tea",
  "teaId": "lydia-house",
  "text": "She heard one sermon by a river and then strong-armed the apostles into moving in.\n\nActs sixteen. Paul and his companions get to Philippi, and on the sabbath they go out of the city by a river side, where prayer was made. They sit down and speak to the women who gathered there.\n\nAnd there's Lydia. Seller of purple, from Thyatira. Purple is the luxury trade. She has money and she runs a business.\n\nAnd the text says the Lord opened her heart, that she attended unto the things which were spoken of Paul.\n\nShe's baptized. Her whole household with her.\n\nAnd then she makes an offer that is not really an offer. \"If ye have judged me to be faithful to the Lord, come into my house, and abide there.\"\n\nAnd Luke adds four words that tell you everything. \"And she constrained us.\"\n\nShe talked them into it. That is the phrasing. She would not take no.\n\nAnd here's the receipt. Later in that same chapter, after Paul and Silas get out of prison, where do they go? They entered into the house of Lydia.\n\nHer house was the base of operations. Not asked. Told.",
